WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.041
"The Best Dietary Detox"

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.560
We lack robust safety data

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:12.120
on most of the estimated
30,000 chemicals

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:13.360
in wide commercial use

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:17.400
registered under the U.S.
Toxic Substances Control Act.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.000
But the greatest concern may lie

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.400
in the long-banned
legacy chemicals

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.000
that continue to contaminate
the food supply

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.440
known as PLOPs-persistent
lipophilic organic pollutants.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:33.560
These include dioxins, PCBs,
and insecticides such as DDT.

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:36.000
How do we drop the PLOPs?

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.440
Today, most DDT
comes from meat,

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:39.800
particularly fish.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:42.520
The oceans are essentially
humanity's sewer;

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:45.960
everything eventually flows
into the sea.

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.040
Hexachlorobenzene is
another banned pesticide

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:50.440
that may be carcinogenic,

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:54.360
but is more evenly spread
among animal food sources,

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:57.640
whereas PCBs are
also mostly a fish thing.

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:00.520
PCBs are a different set
of banned chemicals,

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:02.480
once widely used
as insulating fluid

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:04.160
in electrical equipment.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:06.760
A study of more than 12,000
food and feed samples

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:08.320
across 18 countries

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:10.360
found that the highest
PCB contamination

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:12.480
was found in fish and fish oil,

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:15.200
followed by eggs, then dairy,
then other meats.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.760
Salmon may have
the highest concentration

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:18.960
(with farmed-raised salmon

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:21.000
having consistently higher
contaminant levels

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:24.280
than wild-caught)
followed by canned tuna.

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:26.880
But since people don't tend
to eat a lot of fish,

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:29.840
other meat may be the largest
exposure for most people.

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:32.480
The lowest contamination
was found

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:35.080
at the bottom
of the food chain in plants,

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:38.880
which can average 7 to 20 times
fewer overall PCB

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:40.120
and dioxin-like chemicals

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:44.120
compared to ocean
or freshwater fish.

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:45.600
That's one of the advantages

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.160
to eating more plant-based
in the modern world.

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:50.440
By eating from the lowest rung
of the food chain,

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:52.960
we suffer less exposure
to the industrial pollutants

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:56.040
that bioaccumulate
up the ladder.

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:57.760
Every year
in the United States,

00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:58.680
billions of pounds

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.960
of slaughterhouse by-products
are produced,

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:02.000
the vast majority of which

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.480
are fed right back
to the farm animals,

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:05.760
particularly chickens,

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.960
which can recycle
toxic heavy metals

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:11.360
and industrial chemicals
back into the food supply.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:12.680
Lead builds up in bones

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:15.160
and mercury attaches
to the protein

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:17.440
(which is why egg whites can
have four times more mercury

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:19.360
than do yolks).

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:20.840
Most of the lead
in the bone meal

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:24.000
passes right through
the animals into their waste,

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:25.920
but then producers
can take that waste-

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:27.440
cow, pig, and chicken feces-

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:30.080
and feed it
back to the animals again.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:32.120
So, you can see
how the levels of contaminants

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:33.680
might build up in their bodies

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:35.240
even when the animals themselves

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:38.160
may be natural herbivores.

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:40.080
Lower pollutant levels
may help explain

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:42.000
why those eating plant-based

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:43.960
appear to be less likely
to develop

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:46.320
all forms of cancer combined,

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:49.720
but their role in longevity
is unknown.

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:51.120
Heavy metals such as lead

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:53.600
appear to accelerate
human aging,

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:55.600
and most population studies
have suggested

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:57.800
a strong association
between exposure

00:02:57.800 --> 00:02:59.800
to higher levels
of environmental pollutants

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:01.440
and shorter telomeres.

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:02.920
However, only a few
have been found

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:06.400
to be significantly related
to premature death.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:07.960
One such contaminant

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:12.320
is the long-banned pesticide
beta-hexachlorocyclohexane.

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:13.400
Higher levels in the blood

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:16.400
correlate with higher
all-cause mortality.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:19.280
A study of the breast milk
from two sisters

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:20.560
with different dietary habits

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:24.440
offered a clue
on a way to lower exposure.

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:27.430
The levels
of beta-hexachlorocyclohexane,

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:29.054
as well as PCBs, DDT,

00:03:29.054 --> 00:03:31.200
and another banned pesticide
dieldrin

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:33.280
were much lower
in the breast milk

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:36.760
from the vegetarian mother
than the milk of her sister,

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:38.490
who was also breastfeeding
at the time,

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:41.200
but included meat in her diet.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:44.240
Studies of the pollutants
in breast milk of vegetarians

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:45.960
dating back over 30 years

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:47.960
have found the average levels
of some pollutants

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:51.480
were 50 to 100 times lower
in the vegetarians

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:53.720
compared
to the national average.

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:55.760
In fact, for the six
out of seven pollutants

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:58.560
they looked at,
there wasn't even an overlap

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:00.000
in the range of scores;

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.680
the highest vegetarian value
was lower

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:06.920
than the lowest value obtained
in the general population.

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:09.760
Chlorinated PCBs
have also been associated

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:12.040
with increased mortality risk,

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:14.560
suggesting we should
minimize exposure,

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:17.760
which basically means
a reduction in animal fats.

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:20.120
The blood of those eating
strictly plant-based diets

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:23.280
were found to be
"significantly less polluted"

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:25.160
regarding a whole series
of PCBs,

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:26.680
including those found
in the study

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:29.240
to be associated
with increased mortality,

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:32.120
but their lower levels
of beta-hexachlorocyclohexane

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:34.920
did not reach
statistical significance.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:36.920
Those eating plant-based diets
have also been found

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:39.920
to have markedly lower levels
of dioxins in their bodies,

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:41.680
as well as decreased
contamination

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:43.480
with flame-retardant
chemical pollutants

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:45.600
known as PBDEs.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:48.520
No surprise given the sources
of flame retardant chemicals

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:50.160
in the food supply.

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:52.040
Again, even though
the highest levels

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:53.920
of flame retardants
in the U.S. food supply

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:55.440
have been found in fish,

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:58.880
the primary source of intake
for most Americans is poultry,

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:00.400
just because we eat
so much chicken,

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:02.640
followed by processed meat.

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:04.360
For some reason, U.S. chickens

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:06.840
are about 10 to 20 times
more contaminated

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:10.080
than chickens tested
from some other countries.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:12.400
The longer people
go without meat,

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:15.240
the lower their levels
appear to fall.

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:16.840
Eating healthier
can also reduce

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:19.720
the concentrations
of heavy metals in your body.

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:21.600
The levels of mercury
in the hair

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:23.200
of those eating
more plant-based diets

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:24.920
were found to be
up to ten times lower

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:26.840
than of those who ate fish,

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:29.600
but you don't know
if it's cause and effect

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:32.600
until you put it to the test.

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:33.840
Within three months
of switching

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:36.760
to a plant-based diet,
the levels of mercury, lead,

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:39.240
and cadmium
growing out in your hair

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:41.920
appear to drop significantly

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:43.480
(but build back up
when meat and eggs

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:45.720
are added back into the diet).

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:47.240
Unlike heavy metals, though,

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:52.240
some organochlorine pollutants
can stick around for decades.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:54.400
A USDA examination
of the levels

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:57.040
of dioxin-like compounds
in U.S. meat and poultry

00:05:57.040 --> 00:06:00.840
indicated a possible concern
for U.S. public health,

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:02.960
but really mostly for children.

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:05.800
The typical U.S. adult
daily exposure in meat

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:08.760
was well below the EPA
established safety limit.

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:10.920
Only children
chronically consuming

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:12.680
the average daily servings
of meat or poultry

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:15.200
with the highest levels
might exceed it.

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:17.600
Taking all 33
chemical pollutants in meat

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:20.600
shown to be potentially
carcinogenic into account,

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:22.320
some European toxicologists

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:24.240
suggest limiting
children's consumption

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:26.040
of beef, pork, and chicken

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:29.440
to a combined total of no more
than five servings a month,

00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:31.440
so an average of no more than
like one serving of meat

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:33.360
every six days or so.

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:36.440
In Europe,
lamb is the most contaminated,

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:38.240
and the recommendation
calls for adults

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:39.800
to eat no more than
a single serving

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:42.560
every four or five months.

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:45.280
Surprisingly, as I explored
in a previous video,

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:47.120
the consumption of organic meat

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:49.760
does not seem to diminish
the cancer-causing potential

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:51.760
associated with the PLOPs
in meat.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:53.840
All samples were found
to be contaminated

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:55.200
with minimal differences

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:58.840
between meat raised organic
versus conventional.

00:06:58.840 --> 00:07:00.840
What can we do
to reduce exposure?

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:02.520
Eat high-fiber foods,

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:04.760
as fiber can bind
to some of the contaminants

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:07.120
and flush them out of the body.

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:09.800
Exercise, as blood levels
of persistent pollutants

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:10.960
have been found to be lower

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:13.320
among physically active
individuals,

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:15.080
perhaps due to sweating,

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:18.160
or due to a potential boost
in detoxing enzymes,

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:20.160
or increased clearance
through the bile,

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:22.080
at least in rats.

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:24.400
Given current
contamination levels,

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:26.200
"meat consumption in general...

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:28.920
should be
significantly modified downward,

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:31.760
as much
and as soon as possible,"

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:34.680
though until then,
consumers can reduce exposures

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:37.440
to dioxins and dioxin-like
compounds like PCBs

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:39.600
by trimming fat
when preparing meat,

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:40.400
and further trim

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:43.480
and thoroughly drain fat
after cooking.

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:45.920
The Best Dietary Detox

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:59.320
is to not tox
in the first place.

